From: =?UTF-8?q?Pablo=20Su=C3=A1rez=20Hern=C3=A1ndez?=
 <psuarezhernandez@suse.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:07:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Honor proxy settings in gitfs, git_pillar and winrepo
 (bsc1261147)

* Add proxy option to gitfs, git_pillar and winrepo

(cherry picked from commit 58f6d2c3a9d7614261e08859580d57e780e092bf)

* Update config files

(cherry picked from commit c798ed6b20990bd3c6b85061efa6ceaa8ad603ec)

* Update documentation

(cherry picked from commit 85d4d48c56a3d20de01b9e503aa0fe9c55c21dcf)

* Add tests and changelog for gitfs proxy support

Cover the parts of the proxy option that were previously untested and
that regressed silently: that ``proxy`` is a valid per-remote override
for all three git roles, that a per-remote value beats the global
default, that the configured proxy is enforced as ``http.proxy`` in the
cached repo's git config (and cleared again when unset), that
``Pygit2._fetch`` enables libgit2's proxy lookup, and that a non-https
remote warns instead of silently bypassing the proxy.

``_prepare_provider`` becomes a factory so the proxy can be varied, and
grows the ``proxy`` per-remote default that ``enforce_git_config`` now
requires.

Also retarget the ``versionadded`` markers at the 3006.x release this
lands in.

Signed-off-by: Ismael Luceno <iluceno@suse.de>

* Add the proxy option to test opts that build git providers

GitBase.__init__ requires a global default for every per-remote
override, so hand-rolled opts dicts have to carry the new
gitfs_proxy/git_pillar_proxy keys or provider setup fails hard.

Signed-off-by: Ismael Luceno <iluceno@suse.de>

* Ignore proxy settings in older version of pygit2

* Adjust tests expectation for old pygit2 version

---------

Signed-off-by: Ismael Luceno <iluceno@suse.de>
